<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kyrgyz Feb unemployment falls to 4.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Kyrgyz Feb unemployment falls to 4.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people unemployed in Kyrgyzstan fell to 72,000 or 4.0 percent of the workforce at the end of February from 78,000 in January, the National Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    KYRGYZ UNEMPLOYMENT	   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>    number unemployed	     72,000     78,000     65,000</p>
<p>    percentage of workforce	4.0	  4.3	  3.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are for those officially registered as unemployed in the former Soviet republic of 4.5 million.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
